{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dihedral-crying-grunion","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nStory anguished-grown-junebug (1783-208c-59e9-4096) removed the visual workflow editor but deliberately left `pyproject.toml` untouched. `scripts/dependency_audit.py:50` (`DEPENDENCY_MAP_FILES`) treats ANY edit to `pyproject.toml` as touching the dependency map (the deliberate, package-blind \"touch it, you own it\" rule from bug 63e8). The committed lock carries HIGH advisories tracked by unhelpful-supersmart-chrysalis (f7dc-132b-057a-476c), including one with no published fix. So the editor-removal change could not pass `pip-audit` with these edits in it. The leftovers are inert: the wheel builds with 0 editor files with them present.\n\n## Approach\nOnce f7dc-132b-057a-476c has cleared the lock advisories, remove the 4 stale hunks in one change. This change touches the dependency map, so `pip-audit` must be green on its patchset.\n\n## Scope\nEdit `pyproject.toml` only (line numbers on origin/main b97d414b8e2):\n1. `:370-373` — the comment block and `\"src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor_assets/dist/**/*\",` entry in `[tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel].artifacts` (the editor bundle glob).\n2. `:382-383` comment and `:388` `\"**/node_modules\",` in the wheel `exclude` list.\n3. `:403` `\"**/node_modules\",` in the sdist `exclude` list.\n4. `:743` the `e2e:` entry in `[tool.pytest.ini_options].markers`, plus the `:546` comment `(prompt_authoring/snapshot) carry justified noqas` reworded to name only the remaining snapshot site.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -n -E 'editor_assets|prompt_authoring|node_modules|\"e2e:' -- pyproject.toml` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `uv build --wheel` succeeds and `unzip -l dist/*.whl | grep -c editor_assets` prints `0`.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change reaches `Verified +1` with the `pip-audit` job green, and `LLM-Review +1`.","id":"3360-ba7a-7e72-4ccc","parent_id":"f041-4a84-fcdf-405a","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Drop 4 stale editor references from pyproject.toml once lock advisories are resolved"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792370276743943160,"uuid":"93c66c24-f604-450d-a971-eca010598f0d"}